{
  "$comment": [
    "The spoke manifest. `tcat-spoke init` writes this FOR you -- run that",
    "instead of editing this by hand, and delete this file when it has.",
    "",
    "It is kept here so the shape is readable before you run anything, and so",
    "the `$comment` blocks can explain the two fields with consequences outside",
    "the validator: `stewards`, which becomes a repository permission, and",
    "`maturity`, which is what everyone else reads to decide how much weight to",
    "put on what is in here."
  ],

  "standard_version": "0.2.0",
  "spoke_id": "REPLACE",
  "kind": "data",
  "name": "REPLACE",

  "granularity": "REPLACE",
  "$comment_granularity": [
    "lab | student | instrument | campaign | sub-project | monorepo | mixed --",
    "or anything else. Nothing validates or joins on this; it exists so the",
    "answer is written down rather than inferred from a directory listing. A",
    "spoke whose granularity changed over time says `mixed`, which is honest."
  ],

  "stewards": [
    { "name": "REPLACE", "institution": "REPLACE", "role": "data_steward",
      "github": "REPLACE", "orcid": "REPLACE" },
    { "name": "REPLACE", "institution": "REPLACE", "role": "instrument_owner",
      "github": "REPLACE", "orcid": "REPLACE" }
  ],
  "$comment_stewards": [
    "THE ONLY BLOCK HERE WITH A CONSEQUENCE OUTSIDE THE VALIDATOR.",
    ".github/CODEOWNERS is GENERATED from it, so a github handle here is a real",
    "repository permission and a typo is a wrong one. Run",
    "`tcat-spoke codeowners` after any change; CI checks the two agree.",
    "",
    "`instrument_owner` is load-bearing: a calibration change is reviewed by",
    "that person, and the review is worthless if nobody knows who it is. They",
    "own the calibrations/ directory in the generated CODEOWNERS.",
    "",
    "Roles: data_steward | instrument_owner | analysis_owner | pi.",
    "Add `credit_roles` (CRediT, ANSI/NISO Z39.104-2022) if you want authorship",
    "contributions recorded -- that is a SEPARATE question from who is on call.",
    "Add `until` when someone is leaving, so the name does not go stale while",
    "still looking answered."
  ],

  "maturity": { "rung": "sandbox" },
  "$comment_maturity": [
    "The default for records here that make no claim of their own. `sandbox`",
    "means: this may be rewritten or deleted without notice and nothing should",
    "depend on it. That is the right answer while you are finding your feet, and",
    "saying so is worth more than a claim you have not earned.",
    "",
    "A SPOKE may only say `sandbox` or `working`. The rungs above rest on facts",
    "about a particular record -- a named reviewer of THAT record, a paper citing",
    "THAT record -- so they are set per record, never inherited.",
    "",
    "It is a floor, not a ceiling: a sandbox spoke may hold one published dataset."
  ],

  "layout": {
    "dataset": ["manifests", "canonical", "raw", "derived"],
    "calibration": ["calibrations"],
    "protocol": ["protocols"],
    "sample": ["samples"]
  },
  "$comment_layout": [
    "The values above ARE the defaults, so this block is redundant unless you",
    "change it. Every entry is a list, so one kind can live in several places.",
    "Directories are walked recursively, so listing a parent is usually enough."
  ],

  "exclude": ["scratch", "notebooks/.ipynb_checkpoints"],
  "strict": false,
  "$comment_strict": [
    "When true, a JSON file whose kind cannot be inferred is an ERROR rather",
    "than a skip. Worth turning on once your layout has settled."
  ],

  "notes": "REPLACE -- how this spoke is organised and why, and anything that changed."
}
